                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A collection of basic minigames presented as 'prototypes' the developer created over the years. The storytelling style is reminiscent of '[url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/303210/The_Beginners_Guide/]The Beginner's Guide[/url]' but it doesn't quite hit the mark when compared. That being said it is very creative in some areas and the voice acting is pretty good, the way the story is woven within the gameplay is one of the better aspects.\n\nThere is a weird control issue that prevented me moving my mouse all the way down which made it awkward to pick up and interact with objects in levels. There is also no save function. The game takes less than one hour to playthrough.",
